# TypeScript

- Strict TypeScript only. Never introduce `any` unless technically unavoidable and explicitly justified.
- Avoid `as`, non-null assertions (`!`) and unsafe casts used only to silence TypeScript.
- Derive types from schemas or shared types (`packages/shared-types`) instead of duplicating equivalent types.

# Components (React Native and Vue)

- Do not store derived values in state (use render-time computation or `computed`).
- Avoid effects/watchers for logic that belongs in render or event handlers.
- No unnecessary global state, no duplicated state; keep components focused.
- Avoid unnecessary client-side fetching and never move server logic to the client.
- Preserve accessibility semantics.
